1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,466
Hello, West Bay Hotel.

2
00:00:01,466 --> 00:00:02,280
Can I help you?

3
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:03,410
Oh, good morning.

4
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:06,800
I'm ringing about your advertisement in the Evening Gazette.

5
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,390
Is that the one for temporary staff?

6
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:10,100
That's right.

7
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:10,454
Yes.

8
00:00:10,454 --> 00:00:14,349
I'm afraid the person who's dealing with that isn't in today,

9
00:00:14,349 --> 00:00:17,890
but can give you the main details if you like.

10
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:18,510
Yes please.

11
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:22,230
Could you tell me what kind of staff you are looking for?

12
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,750
We're looking for waiters at the moment.

13
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,856
There was one post for a cook,

14
00:00:26,856 --> 00:00:28,360
but that's already been taken.

15
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:29,156
Oh right.

16
00:00:29,156 --> 00:00:31,940
Erm, what are the hours of work?

17
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:37,090
There are two different shifts - there's a day shift from 7 to 2

18
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:40,260
and a late shift from 4 till 11.

19
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,900
And can people choose which one they want to do?

20
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:43,602
Not normally,

21
00:00:43,602 --> 00:00:46,760
because everyone would choose the day shift I suppose.

22
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:49,170
You alternate from one week to another.

23
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:49,588
Okay.

24
00:00:49,588 --> 00:00:52,097
I'm just writing all this down.

25
00:00:52,097 --> 00:00:53,770
What about time off?

26
00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:58,893
You get one day off and I think you can negotiate which one you want, it's more

27
00:00:58,893 --> 00:01:00,400
or less up to you.

28
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,800
But it has to be the same one every week.

29
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,530
Do you know what the rates of pay are?

30
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:10,954
Yes, I've got them here, You get ￡5.50 an hour,

31
00:01:10,954 --> 00:01:13,420
and that includes a break.

32
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,570
Do I have to go home to eat or...

33
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:16,563
You don't have to.

34
00:01:16,563 --> 00:01:19,540
You can get a meal in the hotel if you want to,

35
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:22,270
and here's no charge for it so you might as well.

36
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:22,942
Oh good.

37
00:01:22,942 --> 00:01:23,278
Yes,

38
00:01:23,278 --> 00:01:24,287
so let's see.

39
00:01:24,287 --> 00:01:27,983
I'd get er, two hundred and twenty one, no,two hundred

40
00:01:27,983 --> 00:01:30,000
and thirty one pounds a week?

41
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,910
You'd also get tips - our guests tend to be quite generous.

42
00:01:33,910 --> 00:01:37,091
Erm, is there a uniform?

43
00:01:37,091 --> 00:01:39,000
What about clothes?

44
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,968
Yes, I forgot to mention that.

45
00:01:40,968 --> 00:01:44,576
You need to wear a white shirt, just a plain one,

46
00:01:44,576 --> 00:01:45,560
and dark trousers.

47
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:48,126
You know, not green or anything like that.

48
00:01:48,126 --> 00:01:49,730
And we don't supply those.

49
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:53,440
That's okay, I've got trousers, I'd just have to buy a couple of shirts.

50
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:54,524
What about anything else?

51
00:01:54,524 --> 00:01:56,420
Do I need a waistcoat or anything?

52
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,920
You have to wear a jacket,

53
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,420
but the hotel lends you that.

54
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,103
I see.

55
00:02:00,103 --> 00:02:04,200
Er, one last thing - I don't know what the starting date is.

56
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:09,276
Just a minute, I think it's some time around the end of June.

57
00:02:09,276 --> 00:02:12,400
Yes, the 28th, in time for the summer.

58
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:13,086
That's great.

59
00:02:13,086 --> 00:02:14,800
I'm available from the 10th.

60
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,438
Oh good.

61
00:02:15,438 --> 00:02:19,900
Well, if you can call again you need to speak to the Service Manager.

62
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,429
Her name's Jane Urwin,

63
00:02:22,429 --> 00:02:23,694
that's U-R-W-I-N,

64
00:02:23,694 --> 00:02:28,120
and she'll probably arrange to meet you.

65
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:28,499
Okay.

66
00:02:28,499 --> 00:02:31,150
And when's the best time to ring?

67
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,573
Could you call tomorrow?

68
00:02:32,573 --> 00:02:35,775
Urn, she usually starts checking the rooms at midday,

69
00:02:35,775 --> 00:02:37,910
so before then if you can,

70
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,400
so she'll have more time to chat.

71
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,920
I'll just give you her number because she's got a direct line.

72
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:44,560
Thanks.

73
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:48,090
It's 832 double-0 9.

74
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:51,000
823 double-0 9?

75
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,200
832.

76
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,043
Oh, okay.

77
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:55,730
Yes, I'll do that.

78
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:58,442
And by the way, she will ask you for a reference,

79
00:02:58,442 --> 00:03:00,660
so you might like to be thinking about that.

80
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:03,720
You know, just someone who knows you and can vouch for you.

81
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,683
Yes, no problem.

82
00:03:04,683 --> 00:03:06,930
Well, thanks very much for your help.

83
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:07,910
You're welcome.

84
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:08,400
Bye.

85
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,290
Bye.
